        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "The public records identify **MO-25-09-1070** (**WO-2025-09-004**, Cooler Plate Pack, Racine) in the September 2025 cost period. That period entered **Pending Close at 2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI could not verify whether an event was created after that time, or retrieve its source transaction, amount, event-created time, or recorded accounting status. The public records contain no event rows, and the supporting records and mirrored attachment are restricted to a records-custodian role. Consequently, I cannot calculate lateness or determine whether a recorded status is consistent with the policy. The available Oracle policy excerpt says transactions created after Pending Close are not processed until the period is closed or reopened.\n\nI submitted the report with the access limitation documented; its receipt is **needs_evidence**. No database records were changed.",
